What's your tape device that are you using?

You want to make sure to specify the no-rewind tape device such as
/dev/nrmt0a versus /dev/rmt0a.

I'm using

    /sbin/vdump -q -0u -N -f /dev/nrmt0a -b 64 FILESYSTEM_NAME

and I can back up multiples without a problem.

When you want to restore, use the <mt> command to position the tape in the
correct file system and you are set.

Dale


