poyae@my-deja.com wrote:

> Hi,
>
> I am using a Compaq AlfaServer ES40 and using True64 v.4.0F.
> It is a totally new box and I am using Customer installation with UFS.
> After a Full installation when it should automatically boot it
> complains with following message:
>
> Bootstrap address collision, image loading aborted
>
>  halted CPU 0
>
>  halt code = 5
>  HALT instruction executed
>  PC = 20010530
>  boot failure
>  P00>>>

This means the kernel's load address is such that it would
step on the console's memory. The most common cause is the
console grew past the 2MB limit but the kernel wasn't
relinked.  V4.0F requires a patch before the console can
be allowed to grow past 2mb.

Please verify the following:

1) Verify the generic kernel boots:

 P00>>>b -fi genvmunix

2) Show the console's heap size and sent it to me:

 P00>>>show heap_expand

3) Show the console's memory descriptors and send me
   the output:

 P00>>>show hwrpb

 This is the part we need......

00002D40        memory descriptor
        40000000 E051AF0D CHECKSUM
        00000000 00000000 IMP_DATA_PA
        00000000 00000005 CLUSTER_COUNT

        00000000 00000000 START_PFN
        00000000 00000100 PFN_COUNT
        00000000 00000000 TEST_COUNT
        00000000 00000000 BITMAP_VA
        00000000 00000000 BITMAP_PA
        00000000 00000000 BITMAP_CHKSUM
        00000000 00000001 USAGE
                        0 bad page(s)

        00000000 00000100 START_PFN
        00000000 0001FE81 PFN_COUNT
        00000000 0001FE81 TEST_COUNT
        00000000 10210000 BITMAP_VA
        00000000 3FF14000 BITMAP_PA
        FFFFFFFF FFFFF807 BITMAP_CHKSUM
        00000000 00000000 USAGE
                        0 bad page(s)

Assuming the generic kernel boots, the try this as a
workaround:

Login as root.

edit the file /usr/sys/conf/MACHINE (where MACHINE is
the hostname in upper case).

Search for a line beginning with "#makeoptions" or
"makeoptions".  Insert the following line:

makeoptions LOADADDR="fffffc0000430000"

relink the kernel:

doconfig -c MACHINE

install the new kernel:

cp /sys/MACHINE/vmunix /vmunix

shutdown the system and reboot

shutdown -h now

P00>>> boot






