You can control the memory size on SRM console with "show mem", then boot up
Tru64 UNIX, and when the System is up you can control with "uerf -R -r 300 �
more" or if decevent is installed "dia -R � more"  if Unix sees the new
memories.

but to better implement the new memory size in Tru64 you need to adapt the
swap space, and you can run a "sys_check -all". The sys_check gives you some
tips of kernel parameter settings for a better memory adaptation..

