Let me clarify: I should have said that DEC/CPQ does not support
internal/external SCSI devices on the same adapter. That might be the 
KZPBA (Qlogic 1040) or the onboard one.

The reason is the cable length issue, and the fact that flatcables
(internal) and round cables (external) in some cases have sufficiently
different impedances etc to cause trouble on high speed buses. 

So you might be able to get away with it, but if it does not work CPQ will
not support it.

