Paul Francis (xyz@xyz.com) wrote:
: Also it should be possible to use dd if you want to make an image backup
: onto an identical disk. You simply copy from one disk onto the other.

Unfortunately, the "simply" part will not work under Tru64: the disk label
(block 0) is write-protected from accesses via the regular block ro character
device writes, and has to be written by disklabel. However, something like:

dd if=/dev/rrz8c bs=1k count=63 iseek=1 oseek=1 of=/dev/rrz9c
dd if=/dev/rrz8c bs=64k iseek=1 oseek=1 of=/dev/rrz9c

works Ok.

