Miguel Demaerel  <Miguel.Demaerel@SGMS.SEMA.BE> wrote:
> Hoi
> 
> How can I change the hostname?
> The hostname is van1.van.org but I wont van1 (without van.org)
> 
> I have done hostname van1
> In the /etc/hosts     ipadres van1

Don't do that.  Stick with

ipaddress	fully-qualified-real-name	short-name alias1 alias2 ... aliasn

> But when I reboot it is back van1.van.org

You only need to edit /etc/rc.config and change the HOSTNAME to the short
version.  You can do this with an editor or with the 

	rcmgr set HOSTNAME van1

command.  Then just run

	hostname van1

as root, and it's done.

Tim
