Don't make the mistake of assuming that just because we use UNIX, we're
immune to this class of virii.  It just requires more stupidity on the
part of the end user, since there hasn't been as much stupidity on the
part of the programmers.

Example:  it could be seen as a good thing to automatically display a
PostScript image attached to one's email, so one might set up mutt to
run ghostscript on attachments with the appropriate MIME type.  Joe
Malicious sends me a postscript attachment, and I blithely bring that
sucker up... whoops.  It's theoretically possible to write a PS virus.

