Usually, a look at the front of the box will yield a clue to the speed.  For
example, the box under my desk asys "Alphastation 400 4/233", which indicates
that it's an Alphastation 400, with an EV4 processor running at 233Mhz.

The command "uerf -Rr 300" will yield the hardware information from the most
recent boot - a clue might be in there.

Finally, the "psrinfo -v" command will probably tell you what you want to
know.

