Hi.

We recently upgraded a DEC (well, it was DEC when we bought it:-)
AlphaServer 1000 from Digital Unix 4.0F to Tru64 Unix 5.0.  In
addition, we have a lab that contains about two dozen NCD XTerminals.

Students use the NCDs to do an xdm-based login on the TruUnix
machine.  The students' .xsession files invoke a window manager
(fvwm95-2, FWIW). 

Prior to the upgrade, this all worked fine.  Post upgrade, there's a
problem.  It seems that fvwm95-2 notices that a window manager (the
NCD Window Manager) is running, and the xdm session gets clobbered.

Note that the NCD Window Manager is running directly on the
XTerminals, and not on the TruUnix box.  This means that (for
instance) the Xsession file can't search for an NCD Window Manager
process and kill it.

Does anybody have any idea how to fix this?  Currently, we are telling
students to disable the NCD Window Manager by hand before doing the
xdm login, but this is inelegant, to say the least.

Thanks.

