First Whatever you do backup first... That removes the worry over destroying
data.

What filesystem do you have on /usr if the answer is ufs the I think you are
out of luck, and the process is ...
backup the whole disk
boot from other media (cd if nothing else)
repartition as required
restore data

If the answer is AdVFS, then you still can't change the partition size without
loosing data, but you can add partitions to the domain making it bigger.


Hope this helps.
