In article <8eustj$6og$1@nnrp1.deja.com>, Young Song
<yssong@ocf.berkeley.edu> wrote:
>I tried using dtadvfs to rename an existing AdvFS filedomain but
>it told me that the filedomain is mounted and thus cannot be
>renamed or so but it's actually not.
>
>Could anyone knowledgeable on Tru64 teach me how to do that?

The name of the domain is the name of its directory entry in
/etc/fdmns.  

Make sure that all filesets in the domain have been unmounted.  If all
the filesets are unmounted, then when you do a 'showfdmn domain_name'
you should get a message such as the following:

    showfdmn: unable to display volume info; domain not active

Use the mvdir command to rename the domain to whatever you like.  

After you rename the directory, make sure that you change your
/etc/fstab file to specify the new domain name, and any other scripts
you may have that reference the old domain name.



